-- title:
--   Special-fibre coordinates pass to a tensor product of towers
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime, and fix an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbf Z/p$. Let $(R_v)_{v\in\mathbb N}$ be commutative $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $t_v\colon R_{v+1}\to R_v$, let $\sigma$ be a finite type, and let $x_v\colon\sigma\to R_v$ satisfy: $t_v(x_{v+1,i})=x_{v,i}$ for all $v,i$; each $x_{v,i}$ lies in the radical of the ideal $(p)\subseteq R_v$; for each $v$ the $\mathbf Z/p$-algebra map $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,\sigma\,(\mathbf Z/p)\to (\mathbf Z/p)\otimes_{\mathcal O}R_v$ sending $X_i\mapsto 1\otimes x_{v,i}$ is surjective; and for every $N$ there is a $v$ for which the kernel of that map is contained in the $N$-th power of the ideal generated by all the $X_i$. Let $(R'_v,t'_v,\sigma',x'_v)$ be a second such datum, satisfying the same four conditions. The conclusion is the conjunction of the corresponding four statements for the tower $R_v\otimes_{\mathcal O}R'_v$ with transition maps $\mathrm{map}(t_v,t'_v)$, index type $\sigma\oplus\sigma'$, and elements given by $\mathrm{Sum.elim}$ of $i\mapsto x_{v,i}\otimes 1$ and $i\mapsto 1\otimes x'_{v,i}$: compatibility with the transition maps, membership in the radical of $(p)\subseteq R_v\otimes_{\mathcal O}R'_v$, surjectivity of the induced map from $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\sigma\oplus\sigma')\,(\mathbf Z/p)$ to $(\mathbf Z/p)\otimes_{\mathcal O}(R_v\otimes_{\mathcal O}R'_v)$, and, for every $N$, existence of a $v$ whose kernel lies in the $N$-th power of the ideal generated by the variables.
--
--   The four conditions packaged here are the hypotheses of the criterion identifying the inverse limit of a tower of $\mathcal O$-algebras with a power series ring in the variables indexed by $\sigma$; the statement says that this package is stable under forming the tensor product of two towers. It is used in the construction of the multivariate formal group law attached to the connected component of a $p$-divisible group, where the criterion must be applied to $\Gamma^0\times\Gamma^0$ and to $\Gamma^0\times\Gamma^0\times\Gamma^0$ in order to interpret the comultiplication and to verify associativity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_TensorProduct_specialFibre_coordinates_sumElim_tmul.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
